=== J4. Reduction along s(X), n = 4 (closed forms of F2-F6; exact sympy) ===
  Z1: on s(X), Ric(g) = Lambda_g g:  G^Y = ((-4*Lambda_g*c_V*(4*lambda - 1) + 5*c_H*(18*lambda - 5) + c_H)/(4*c_H*c_V*(4*lambda - 1))) h + ((-16*Lambda_g*c_V*lambda + 4*Lambda_g*c_V + 35*c_H*lambda - 10*c_H)/(2*c_H*(4*lambda - 1))) G_0 + ((c_H*(4*lambda - 1) + lambda*(8*Lambda_g*c_V*(4*lambda - 1) + 5*c_H*(5 - 18*lambda)))/(4*c_H*(4*lambda - 1))) tau(x)tau  (h = c_H g on H),  Lambda_P = 3*c_H*(15*lambda - 4)/(2*c_V*(4*lambda - 1));  Hess of a function with dt = a tau, t const on s(X): HH = (1/(2*c_V*(1 - 4*lambda))) a h
  Z2: on s(X), Ric(g) = Lambda_g g:  G^Y = (-Lambda_g/c_H + 9/(2*c_V)) h + (-2*Lambda_g*c_V/c_H + 7/2) G_0 + ((c_H + 2*lambda*(4*Lambda_g*c_V - 9*c_H))/(4*c_H)) tau(x)tau  (h = c_H g on H),  Lambda_P = 9*c_H/(2*c_V);  Hess of a function with dt = a tau, t const on s(X): HH = (0) a h
  (B) basic t = pi^* tau, u = pi^* upsilon.  On s(X): Hess_HH = Hess_g, Hess_VV = 0 (fibres totally geodesic, F3/F4(a)), Hess(X, U) = 0 (Z2: A = 0) or g_aleph(II(X, grad phi), U) (Z1, F4(a)); dphi horizontal.
    (P) keeps the HH and HV blocks: Z2 -> the 4D system  -x_i (G(g) + Lambda_P g) + c_H c_i g + sum H_i,phi (nabla^2 tau_phi - Box tau_phi g) + sum Q dtau dtau + sum Q' <dtau,dtau> g = 0 (i = 1, 13) and varpi dtau ^ dupsilon = 0 (coefficients of J2, unchanged); Z1 -> in addition HV:  II(X, H_i,t grad tau + H_i,u grad upsilon) = 0, i.e. H (dtau, dupsilon)^T = 0.
    (E) adds the VV block, -x_i G^Y_VV + (scalar) g_VV = 0:  needs Ric^Y_VV proportional to g_VV, i.e. Z1 with lambda = 1/5 (F6) when (x, y) != 0; and HV as in (P)-Z1.
  (J) isotropy-invariant 2-jet along s(X): t, u constant on s(X), dphi = a_phi tau (a const), Hess phi = beta_phi h + p_phi G_0 + q_phi tau(x)tau with beta_phi = beta a_phi; G(g) traceless part must vanish (g Einstein) when (x, y) != 0.
